{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01X5pfmiMSEcrc92C18kW2o9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils is a specification-driven experiment that derives formal specs from C source code, generates Go implementations of Unix utilities via AI, and verifies parity against GNU reference binaries through differential testing.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Key components: `cmd/` (per-utility Go implementations), `pkg/sys/` (platform syscall wrappers), `pkg/format/` (output formatting), `pkg/testutils/` (differential testing harness), `magefiles/` (build targets), `docs/` (human-authored specs).\n\n**Current state**: Source code exists for `pkg/testutils`, `pkg/sys`, `pkg/format`, `cmd/cat` (with tests), `cmd/wc` (with tests), `cmd/sponge` (implementation only, no tests), and `cmd/du` (implementation only, no tests). All specs for releases 00.0 through 01.3 are complete.\n\n**Current release priority**: rel01.2 (sponge) is the earliest release with incomplete work -- `cmd/sponge/main.go` exists but no test file. rel01.3 (du) is in the same state.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nFollowing P1 (release-driven priority), rel01.2-uc001-sponge is the earliest incomplete use case with actionable work. The implementation exists (`cmd/sponge/main.go`), but differential tests are missing. Per P5 (dependency ordering), tests follow implementation, and the implementation is already present.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Implement differential tests for cmd/sponge (prd007-sponge R1-R5)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd007-sponge.yaml (sponge requirements and acceptance criteria)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-01.2.yaml (test suite spec for sponge release)\n      - cmd/sponge/main.go (implementation under test -- review all flags and behaviors)\n      - cmd/cat/cat_test.go (TestMain pattern and RunDiffTests usage reference)\n      - cmd/wc/wc_test.go (additional TestMain and differential test pattern reference)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests API)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/sponge/sponge_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Differential tests for sponge against Homebrew moreutils reference binary\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement TestMain that locates the reference binary 'sponge' (Homebrew moreutils) via exec.LookPath, builds the Go sponge binary from the current package to a temp directory, and cleans up after tests complete. Skip all tests gracefully (os.Exit(0) with message) if the reference binary is not found on PATH. Follow the exact TestMain pattern from cmd/cat/cat_test.go.\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement passthrough mode tests (prd007-sponge R4) using pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests. Test stdin-to-stdout behavior when no output file argument is given: empty stdin, simple text, multi-line input, and binary data. These tests compare stdout, stderr, and exit code between the Go and reference binaries.\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement file output mode tests (prd007-sponge R1, R2). Run both Go and reference binaries with a temp output file argument, piping identical stdin to each. After execution, compare the output files byte-for-byte and compare stderr and exit codes. Test cases: simple write to new file, overwrite of existing file, and write with stdin containing no trailing newline.\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement append mode tests (prd007-sponge R3). Test the -a flag by creating an existing file with known content, running both binaries with -a and the same stdin, then comparing the resulting file contents. Verify that original content is preserved and new content is appended.\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"The reference binary name is 'sponge' (Homebrew moreutils, no g-prefix). moreutils binaries do not conflict with macOS built-ins and are not g-prefixed.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Use pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests for passthrough mode tests where sponge writes to stdout. For file output mode tests, run each binary separately using exec.Command with identical stdin and environment, then compare the output files byte-for-byte and stderr/exit code manually, since RunDiffTests only compares stdout, stderr, and exit code.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Follow the TestMain build pattern from cmd/cat/cat_test.go: build the Go binary with exec.Command('go', 'build', '-o', goBinaryPath, '.'), store paths in package-level vars goBinaryPath and refBinaryPath, clean up the temp directory after m.Run().\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"Set LC_ALL=C in the environment for all test executions, consistent with the project-wide locale constraint (ARCHITECTURE.yaml DD6). For file output tests that run binaries directly via exec.Command, set the environment explicitly.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"cmd/sponge/sponge_test.go compiles without errors (go build ./cmd/sponge/ succeeds)\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"Tests skip gracefully with a descriptive message when the sponge reference binary is not found on PATH\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"Tests cover passthrough mode (no file argument), file output mode (write to named file), and append mode (-a flag)\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/sponge/ passes when both the Go binary and the sponge reference binary are available\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":71108,"cache_read_input_tokens":19289,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":71108},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"se